Subject: select CUPS system configuration from UAPI directories
Source: Nex downstream patch for CUPS 2.4.7
Upstream: not submitted; needs agreement on Unix vendor and transient paths

Select the scheduler's two complete configuration files and both SNMP readers
from /etc, /run, or /usr/lib. Preserve explicit command-line and environment
paths, including CUPS's privilege checks. Empty higher files deliberately mask
lower defaults.

Share one selector across every reader. cupsd and the two SNMP readers already
followed the tiers, but cupsfilter, the client.conf reader, the cupsd.conf
reader behind cupsctl and the admin CGI, and the mailto notifier each rebuilt
the path from the compiled CUPS_SERVERROOT, so a vendor or transient file was
visible to the scheduler and invisible to them. Add _cupsSystemConfigFile() to
libcups, move the SNMP reader onto it, and use it from all four.
